            "text": "{\"strengths\":[\"The diagram is clear and correctly labels the wheat price and quantity axes, demand, both supply curves, and the two equilibria.\",\"It correctly shows unchanged demand and a leftward shift of supply from S1 to S2, leading to P2 > P1 and Q2 < Q1.\",\"The written response correctly identifies that the equilibrium price rises.\"],\"improvements\":[\"State the causal mechanism explicitly: the drought reduces harvests, so supply decreases at every price.\",\"Complete the written outcome by explaining that equilibrium quantity of wheat falls as well as price rising.\"],\"mistakes\":[\"Incorrect diagram explanation\"],\"examinerComment\":\"Estimated practice mark: 3/4. Your diagram fully communicates the supply contraction and the resulting higher price and lower equilibrium quantity. Your written explanation receives partial credit because it mentions only the higher price; add the reduction in supply and the fall in equilibrium quantity.\",\"studyNext\":\"Practise linking a supply decrease to a shortage at the original equilibrium price, followed by a rise in price and a fall in quantity traded.\",\"assessmentFormat\":\"paper_2_c_to_f_diagram_and_explanation\",\"paper\":\"paper_2\",\"questionPart\":\"unknown\",\"levelRelevance\":\"shared_sl_hl\",\"assessmentSkills\":[\"diagram_explanation\",\"economic_analysis\"],\"commandTerm\":\"explain\",\"commandTermLabel\":\"explain\",\"syllabusUnit\":\"unit_2\",\"syllabusTopic\":\"2.3\",\"topicLabel\":\"Competitive market equilibrium\",\"classificationConfidence\":\"high\",\"markingConfidence\":\"high\",\"diagramExpected\":true,\"diagramSubmitted\":true,\"diagramAssessmentStatus\":\"submitted_and_assessed\",\"workingsExpected\":false,\"workingsSubmitted\":false,\"workingsAssessmentStatus\":\"not_relevant\",\"attachmentContent\":\"diagram\",\"assessableEarned\":3,\"markBreakdown\":[{\"label\":\"Diagram\",\"awarded\":4,\"available\":4,\"reason\":\"The submitted diagram correctly shows unchanged demand, supply shifting left from S1 to S2, and equilibria with higher price and lower quantity.\"},{\"label\":\"Economic analysis\",\"awarded\":2,\"available\":4,\"reason\":\"The answer correctly states that price is higher, but it does not explain that drought reduces supply or state that equilibrium quantity falls.\"}],\"bandRationale\":null,\"limitations\":[],\"componentEvaluation\":{\"diagram\":2,\"explanation\":1,\"diagramReason\":\"A readable and correctly labelled wheat-market diagram shows D unchanged, S1 shifting left to S2, and equilibria indicating P2>P1 and Q2<Q1.\",\"explanationReason\":\"The written response correctly identifies the higher price, but does not complete the causal chain from drought to lower supply and lower equilibrium quantity.\",\"incompatibleMechanisms\":false,\"mismatchEvidence\":\"\",\"labelingDeficiency\":false,\"labelingEvidence\":\"\",\"rootErrors\":[]}}"
          }
